  "title": "Millionaire Sent His Mom $3,000 a Month—Came Home Unannounced, Found Her Begging for Rice on Credit",
  "description": "She apologized for eating. In her own house.<br><br>For three years, Dalton Whitlock sent his mother $3,000 on the first of every month from Dubai. Then he flew home two weeks early without telling anyone, and found Loretta, seventy years old, at Opal&apos;s General Store in Millbrook, Georgia, short on coins for a pound of rice she had been buying on credit for seven months. At her house, a brass padlock hung on the pantry door. His wife, Celeste, kept the key.<br><br>Under her mattress, Dalton found a composition book, written one slow letter at a time. At the bank, he found where his money really went: a joint account, his wife&apos;s sister Brandi, and three loans in his mother&apos;s name she never signed. Her sewing machine had been sold. Her phone had been blocked for five months. And from inside a hall closet, he heard his wife lean across the kitchen table and tell his mother: &quot;Nobody believes a confused old woman.&quot; So he stayed hidden until his daughter&apos;s graduation party, where everyone Celeste ever lied to would be in one room.<br><br>👉 Watch till the end — the woman they called confused finally speaks for herself.<br><br>If you love stories where a forgotten mother is finally seen and the people who used her face what they did, subscribe for a new story every week.<br><br>This is a fictional story made for entertainment. All characters, places and events are invented.<br><br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/familydrama\">#FamilyDrama</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/karma\">#Karma</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/story\">#Story</a>",
